{"id":"NCT06641414","title":"Lisaftoclax (APG-2575) Combined With Azacytidine (AZA) in the Treatment of Patients With Higher-risk Myelodysplastic Syndrome (GLORA-4).","official":"A Global Multicenter, Double-blind, Randomized, Registrational Phase 3 Study of Lisaftoclax (APG-2575) in Combination With Azacitidine (AZA) in Patients With Newly Diagnosed Higher Risk Myelodysplastic Syndrome (HR-MDS) (GLORA-4).","summary":"A global multicenter, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, pivotal phase III study. To evaluate overall survival (OS) of lisaftoclax (APG-2575) combined with azacitidine (AZA) vs. placebo combined with azacitidine in newly diagnosed patients with HR-MDS.","conditions":["Higher-risk Myelodysplastic Syndrome"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Lisaftoclax (APG-2575)"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Azacitidine Injection"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"Placebo"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n1. Newly diagnosed higher-risk MDS.\n2. ECOG score of ≤2.\n3. Expected survival ≥ 3 months.\n4. Adequate organ function.\n5. Female subjects of potential childbearing potential have a negative urine or serum pregnancy test before dosing. Subjects of childbearing potential as well as their partners voluntarily use contraception deemed effective by the investigator during the treatment period and for at least six months after the last dose of study drug.\n6. Able to understand and voluntarily sign a written informed consent form, which must be signed prior to the performance of any trial-specified study procedures.\n7. Subjects are able to complete study procedures and follow-up examinations.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n1. Concomitant other malignancies or prior malignancies with disease-free intervals of less than 1 year at the time of signing the informed consent.\n2. Have undergone hematopoietic stem cell transplantation.\n3. Use of moderately potent inducers and moderately potent inhibitors of CYP3A4 within 14 days prior to the first dose of study drug.\n4. MDS or other conditions that cannot be administered enterally.\n5. Any condition that the subject is deemed to be inappropriate to participate in this study after evaluation by the investigator.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":490,"start":"2025-01-22","pcd":"2029-06","upd":"2026-10-13","sponsor":"Ascentage Pharma Group Inc.","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Yifan Zhai, M.D., Ph.D. · +86-20-28068501 · yzhai@ascentage.com","Qian Niu, M.D. · Qian.Niu@ascentage.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35294","s":"NYR","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85054","s":"R","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90095","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site","city":"Sacramento","pr":"California","zip":"95817","s":"R","lat":38.5816,"lon":-121.4944,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site","city":"San Diego","pr":"California","zip":"92093","s":"R","lat":32.7157,"lon":-117.1647,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site","city":"Aurora","pr":"Colorado","zip":"80045","s":"R","lat":39.7294,"lon":-104.8319,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site","city":"Jacksonville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32224","s":"R","lat":30.3322,"lon":-81.6556,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60611","s":"R","lat":41.85,"lon":-87.65,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site","city":"Indianapolis","pr":"Indiana","zip":"46237","s":"R","lat":39.7684,"lon":-86.158,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage","city":"Iowa City","pr":"Iowa","zip":"52242","s":"NYR","lat":41.6611,"lon":-91.5302,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage Investigative Site","city":"Louisville","pr":"Kentucky","zip":"40202","s":"R","lat":38.2542,"lon":-85.7594,"c":""},{"f":"Ascentage I